    <description>Releases an ABANDONED booking payment hold on a unit when it expires, replacing the sweep that CheckoutPaymentPoller.releaseExpiredBookingHolds used to do (that poller is unscheduled). One scheduled path per hold, firing at that hold&apos;s own expiry - nothing runs on a timer. Purely cosmetic: the hold is time-boxed and every consumer already evaluates Payment_Hold_Expiry__c live, so the unit is free on expiry whether or not this runs. Re-checks at execution so it never clears a RENEWED hold (a later expiry was written) and never touches a unit that reached Reserved or Sold - those succeeded, and UnitBookingJourneyController.releasePaymentHold owns that path. Standard UAE only. MSC-218 (2 Sep 2026): a hold with NO expiry is released immediately instead of being ignored forever. Every safety net here was anchored to the expiry date - this flow only armed when one existed, and CheckoutPaymentPoller sweeps expiry &lt; now - so &quot;in progress = true, expiry = null&quot; was the one state nothing could ever clean up: a permanent hold that hides the unit from every channel (2 units in DEV_1). The entry filter no longer demands an expiry, and an immediate path (Hold has no expiry) releases the malformed ones down the SAME release + fee-line cleanup used by the scheduled path. A hold that carries an expiry is untouched by the new path and still belongs to the scheduled one.</description>
